From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Markus Handell <handellm@webrtc.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:36:25 +0200
Subject: VideoFrameBuffer: introduce ToI420ForInspection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Under pure-hardware-encoding conditions, corruption detection
will receive kUnknown video frame buffers which it inspects using
ToI420. This triggers a readback signal in Chromium which forces
the vide pipeline to read back frame information. This leads to
reconfigurations of hardware encoders in chromium.

Fix this by introducing ToI420ForInspection that will not trigger
readbacks.

Bug: chromium:555719593
Change-Id: Ic14e32ebd98578e9e5034b2a0a927e423164b5e6
Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503522
Reviewed-by: Henrik Boström <hbos@webrtc.org>
Reviewed-by: Erik Språng <sprang@webrtc.org>
Commit-Queue: Erik Språng <sprang@webrtc.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48608}

